- <any other prerequisites, e.g. an API key, a package the user must install first>

## Install

```bash
omarchy plugin add https://github.com/<user>/<repo>.git --enable
```

Omarchy will show a trust warning before installing — plugins run as
arbitrary, unsandboxed code inside the long-lived shell process, with
everything your user account can reach. Review the source first. Installing
clones this repo into `~/.config/omarchy/plugins/<username.pluginname>/`;
it never runs an install hook and never asks for sudo.

## Update

```bash
omarchy plugin update <username.pluginname>
```

## Remove

```bash
omarchy plugin remove <username.pluginname>
```

